{
  "_doc": "SPEECH ACTS (Phase 060): the vocabulary of speech a resident can place, and the switch for a simple resident to act on what it hears. The rows are read by domains/speech_grammar.py (the deterministic grammar) and bigville/backends/speech_in.py (the listener); domains/speech_acts_check.py checks them against the surface templates (conversation.DEFAULT_TEMPLATES), the realised meanings (bigville/runtime.py _realize_meaning) and the acts the simple speakers emit (speech.py _meaning, cheap.py _speech).\n\nROW FIELDS. act: the name, as in the raw payload's `act`. slots: slot name to kind (name, text, word, question; see speech_grammar.py). description: plain words. understood_by: `simple` when a simple resident can place the act from text or raw payload; `none` when it is only sent (no pattern). emitted_by: which speaker emits it. `simple_meaning` is DeterministicSpeechBackend._meaning (the Ocelot mind's and board game seam); `simple_message` is a message the simple backend sends (cheap.py _speech, and speech_in's replies); `message` is a templated world message no simple resident sends yet. template: a key of conversation.DEFAULT_TEMPLATES that renders the act, or null. meaning: the keys of runtime _realize_meaning that render it as a meaning, or []. A row needs a template or a meaning (the self-test's rule). patterns: the extra wordings the grammar places, besides the template's own wording (a template that is only a slot, such as \"{answer}\", gives no pattern). lexicon: pack tables whose phrases are patterns, with lexicon_slot naming the slot the phrases' placeholders fill.\n\nROW ORDER is the grammar's priority: the first matching row wins. Rows with understood_by none carry no patterns.\n\nSPEECH_UNDERSTANDING. enabled: false by default. With it off the simple backend ignores what it hears, and its village is the same as before this phase (checked by tests/test_phase060_speech_in.py). effects: the tunables of what a heard act does. words: the sentences a simple resident says in reply. Each one is also a pattern of the answer act, so the grammar places a reply the same way it places any other answer.\n\nSOURCES. None of the numbers in SPEECH_UNDERSTANDING.effects is a measured figure: each is an APPROX model choice, marked in its comment key, and to be read against the measurements in docs/phases/phase060. The cheap backend's eat threshold, hunger 0.25 (cheap.py _update_goals), is the source of need_hunger. The acts and wordings are the repository's own templates and realisations, not a sourced vocabulary.",
